sure":"st_region_geometry"}]},{"sub":[{"args":[{"var":"x"},{"lit":"y"}],"measure":"kin_position"},{"args":[{"var":"r"},{"lit":"y"}],"measure":"st_region_geometry"}]}]}]},{"mul":[{"args":[{"var":"x"}],"measure":"kin_speed"},{"args":[{"var":"x"}],"measure":"kin_speed"}]}]}]}}]}]},"contract":"A road user moves clockwise about a structure region's reference point at the observation, viewed from above in the world frame, whose positive sense of rotation is counter-clockwise (the sense in which a yaw rate is positive). It holds where the road user is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor) and the cross product of the vector from the region's reference point to the road user's reference point with the road user's velocity is negative and larger in magnitude than sine_tolerance times the product of that vector's length and the road user's speed, compared as squares: the sine of the angle from that radius vector to the velocity is below minus sine_tolerance. The region's reference point is read from st.region_geometry, the road user's from kin.position, its velocity from kin.velocity and its speed from kin.speed, in m and m/s. Motion toward or away from the reference point, within the tolerance, is neither sense. Not denoted: travel against a carrier's designated direction, a change of the road user's heading, or the road user being inside the region: the caller states occupancy.","definition":null,"id":"drv.motion.clockwise_about_region","kind":"formula","narrowings":[],"params":[{"name":"speed_floor","unit":"metre_per_second"},{"name":"sine_tolerance","unit":"ratio"}],"residues":[],"supersedes":null}
